    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nwhen in `nvim` when I press `!` or `]` neovim treats it as `!!` or `]]` respectively, this happens whatever the current mode is (input, normal, visual and commands)\n\nI tested and\n- it only happens in Hyprland, not in KDE\n- it happens with or without my input system on\n- it happens with or without my  nvim config\n- it doesn't happen in any other app (e.g. `vim`)\n- it still happens when I compile it from source on a docker `ubuntu 24.04` on branch `nightly` and `master`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOn NixOs 26.05, Hyprland\n```console\nnvim --clean -u /dev/null # no config needed for the bug\ni!]\n:q!\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect pressing `!` or `]` to be treated as `!` or `]` instead of `!!` or `]]` respectively\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nNixOs 26.05.5591.fd1462031fde\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\ninstalled from nixos stable 26.05 using the nix package manager",
